From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pw4-port <pw4-port@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 17:46:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PW4 Android: mmc_rescan drops its wake lock on every exit

Scheduling the detect work takes the mmc_delayed_work wake lock; the two
early returns of mmc_rescan (rescan disabled, non-removable host already
scanned) left it held until the next full rescan. With the non-removable
Wi-Fi host (0023) that blocked autosuspend after a resume, once for 414 s.
---
 drivers/mmc/core/core.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/core/core.c b/drivers/mmc/core/core.c
index 3eb8d657..2983842b 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/core/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/core/core.c
@@ -2584,12 +2584,18 @@ void mmc_rescan(struct work_struct *work)
 		host->trigger_card_event = false;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * PW4: both early exits used to return without dropping the
+	 * mmc_delayed_work wake lock that scheduling this work took, which
+	 * then blocked autosuspend until the next full rescan (once 414 s
+	 * after a resume, with the non-removable Wi-Fi host).
+	 */
 	if (host->rescan_disable)
-		return;
+		goto out;
 
 	/* If there is a non-removable card registered, only scan once */
 	if ((host->caps & MMC_CAP_NONREMOVABLE) && host->rescan_entered)
-		return;
+		goto out;
 	host->rescan_entered = 1;
 
 	mmc_bus_get(host);
